// expect-error: plain access to 'g_ctr' in a concurrent context
// BUG-916: the atomic-cell rule fired for a FIRE-AND-FORGET spawn and not for a
// SCOPED one, so the same race was accepted purely for its spelling. The rule's
// own comment said post-join access is safe — true — but the code set nothing at
// all, leaving the spawn..join WINDOW unchecked. The spawn body scan does not
// cover it either: @atomic_* is an exemption there.
u32 g_ctr;
void worker() { u32 v = @atomic_add(&g_ctr, 1); }
u32 main() {
    ThreadHandle t = spawn worker();
    g_ctr = 5;
    t.join();
    return 0;
}
